WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.320
A queen dreams that a white elephant
with six tusks enters her side.

2
00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:09.390
Her son grows up with three
palaces: one for the cold,

3
00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:12.240
one for the heat, one for the rains.

4
00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.720
Then, on four outings,
he meets an old man,

5
00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:19.770
a sick man, a corpse, and a calm wanderer.

6
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:23.870
Could a prince really reach
29 without seeing old age?

7
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.660
And why do Buddhists tell it that way?

8
00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:31.190
In this mission, you'll compare the earliest
memories in the Pali Canon with full

9
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.920
life stories written centuries later.

10
00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:37.120
Then you'll test four different
ways of reading the story,

11
00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.360
and what each sight reveals.

12
00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:44.280
Your mission: work out why Buddhists
tell the prince's story the way they do.
